# Vendored third-party assets are checked out exactly as they were published. This
# machine has core.autocrlf=true, which would otherwise rewrite leaflet.js and
# leaflet.css to CRLF on checkout: the bytes would stop matching the upstream release
# an upgrade is supposed to be a straight swap for, and the same file would hash
# differently on a Windows checkout than in CI or production, so the same commit would
# produce two different sets of content-hashed asset names.
gpx/static/gpx/vendor/** -text
